Full rewrite as the SERVED_SET selector — the ONLY reader of the env var in the repo (FD-1/FD-2). Exact content (plan §4.1.3, minus the plant-products entry which lands with pp-007):

import { liveAnimals } from './routes-live-animals.js'

const SETS = { 'live-animals': liveAnimals }

export const servedSetName = () => process.env.SERVED_SET ?? 'live-animals'
export const servedSet = () => {
  const set = SETS[servedSetName()]
  if (!set) throw new Error(`Unknown SERVED_SET "${servedSetName()}"`)
  return set
}

Env read is lazy (at call time, inside the exported functions) — never at module load. Unknown value = loud boot failure, never a silent default. No `export const liveAnimals` re-export from this file (its only importer was router.js, updated below; routes.test.js imports the set's allRoutes directly — verified).
